{"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxldirection"]}],"relationshipsSections":[{"kind":"relationships","identifiers":["doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/s8CopyableP","doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/SQ","doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/s9EscapableP","doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/SH","doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/s8SendableP","doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/s16SendableMetatypeP"],"type":"conformsTo","title":"Conforms To"}],"topicSections":[{"anchor":"Structures","identifiers":["doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLDirection\/Kind-swift.struct"],"generated":true,"title":"Structures"},{"anchor":"Initializers","identifiers":["doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLDirection\/init(id:kind:offset:footnote:level:voice:staff:sound:listening:placement:isDirective:system:)"],"generated":true,"title":"Initializers"},{"anchor":"Instance-Properties","identifiers":["doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLDirection\/footnote","doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLDirection\/id","doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLDirection\/isDirective","doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLDirection\/kind-swift.property","doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLDirection\/level","doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLDirection\/listening","doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLDirection\/offset","doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLDirection\/placement","doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLDirection\/sound","doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLDirection\/staff","doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLDirection\/system","doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLDirection\/voice"],"generated":true,"title":"Instance Properties"},{"anchor":"Default-Implementations","identifiers":["doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLDirection\/Equatable-Implementations"],"generated":true,"title":"Default Implementations"}],"seeAlsoSections":[{"anchor":"Music","identifiers":["doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLMusicItem","doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLNote","doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLRest","doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLPitch","doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLAttributes","doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLBarline","doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLSound"],"generated":true,"title":"Music"}],"kind":"symbol","identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLDirection"},"schemaVersion":{"major":0,"minor":3,"patch":0},"metadata":{"role":"symbol","roleHeading":"Structure","title":"MXLDirection","modules":[{"name":"IvorMXL"}],"externalID":"s:7IvorMXL12MXLDirectionV","symbolKind":"struct","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"MXLDirection"}],"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"MXLDirection"}]},"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL"]]},"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"declarations","declarations":[{"tokens":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"MXLDirection"}],"platforms":["macOS"],"languages":["swift"]}]},{"kind":"content","content":[{"level":2,"text":"Overview","type":"heading","anchor":"overview"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"By default, a series of direction-type elements and a series of child elements of a direction-type within a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"single direction element follow one another in sequence visually. For a series of direction-type children,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"non-positional formatting attributes are carried over from the previous element by default."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Maps the MusicXML "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"<direction>"},{"type":"text","text":" element."}],"type":"paragraph"}]}],"abstract":[{"text":"A direction is a musical indication that is not necessarily attached to a specific note. Two or more may be","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"combined to indicate words followed by the start of a dashed line, the end of a wedge followed by dynamics,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"etc. For applications where a specific direction is indeed attached to a specific note, the direction element","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"can be associated with the first note element that follows it in score order that is not in a different voice.","type":"text"}],"sections":[],"references":{"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLDirection/Kind-swift.struct":{"role":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxldirection\/kind-swift.struct","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLDirection\/Kind-swift.struct","fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Kind","kind":"identifier"}],"kind":"symbol","abstract":[{"text":"Textual direction types may have more than 1 component due to multiple fonts. The dynamics element may also be","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"used in the notations element. Attribute groups related to print suggestions apply to the individual","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"direction-type, not to the overall direction.","type":"text"}],"type":"topic","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"Kind","kind":"identifier"}],"title":"MXLDirection.Kind"},"doc://IvorMXL/SQ":{"type":"unresolvable","title":"Swift.Equatable","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/SQ"},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLAttributes":{"role":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"MXLAttributes","kind":"identifier"}],"fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"MXLAttributes","kind":"identifier"}],"kind":"symbol","title":"MXLAttributes","url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlattributes","type":"topic","abstract":[{"text":"The attributes element contains musical information that typically changes on measure boundaries. This","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"includes key and time signatures, clefs, transpositions, and staving. When attributes are changed mid-measure,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"it affects the music in score order, not in MusicXML document order.","type":"text"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLAttributes"},"doc://IvorMXL/SH":{"type":"unresolvable","title":"Swift.Hashable","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/SH"},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLDirection":{"role":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxldirection","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLDirection","fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"MXLDirection","kind":"identifier"}],"kind":"symbol","abstract":[{"text":"A direction is a musical indication that is not necessarily attached to a specific note. Two or more may be","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"combined to indicate words followed by the start of a dashed line, the end of a wedge followed by dynamics,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"etc. For applications where a specific direction is indeed attached to a specific note, the direction element","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"can be associated with the first note element that follows it in score order that is not in a different voice.","type":"text"}],"type":"topic","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"MXLDirection","kind":"identifier"}],"title":"MXLDirection"},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLDirection/offset":{"title":"offset","fragments":[{"text":"let","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"offset","kind":"identifier"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"MXLOffset","preciseIdentifier":"s:7IvorMXL9MXLOffsetV","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":"?","kind":"text"}],"kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLDirection\/offset","url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxldirection\/offset","role":"symbol","abstract":[{"text":"Indicates where the direction will appear relative to the current musical location, in divisions.","type":"text"}],"type":"topic"},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL":{"type":"topic","abstract":[{"text":"A MusicXML parser, normalizer, validator, and formatter.","type":"text"}],"url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl","title":"IvorMXL","role":"collection","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL","kind":"symbol"},"doc://IvorMXL/s8SendableP":{"title":"Swift.Sendable","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/s8SendableP","type":"unresolvable"},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLNote":{"title":"MXLNote","kind":"symbol","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"MXLNote"}],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Notes are the most common type of MusicXML data. The MusicXML format distinguishes between elements used for"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"sound information and elements used for notation information (e.g., tie is used for sound, tied for notation)."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"Thus grace notes do not have a duration element. Cue notes have a duration element, as do forward elements,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"but no tie elements. Having these two types of information available can make interchange easier, as some"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"programs handle one type of information more readily than the other."}],"type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLNote","role":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"MXLNote"}],"url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlnote"},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLDirection/level":{"url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxldirection\/level","abstract":[{"text":"The level element specifies editorial information for different MusicXML elements. It is defined within a","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"group due to its multiple uses within the MusicXML schema.","type":"text"}],"fragments":[{"text":"let","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"level","kind":"identifier"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"MXLLevel","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:7IvorMXL8MXLLevelV"},{"text":"?","kind":"text"}],"kind":"symbol","role":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLDirection\/level","title":"level","type":"topic"},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLMusicItem":{"role":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlmusicitem","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLMusicItem","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"enum"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"MXLMusicItem"}],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"One of the alternatives for a music item."}],"kind":"symbol","type":"topic","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"MXLMusicItem"}],"title":"MXLMusicItem"},"doc://IvorMXL/s8CopyableP":{"type":"unresolvable","title":"Swift.Copyable","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/s8CopyableP"},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLPitch":{"role":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"MXLPitch","kind":"identifier"}],"fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"MXLPitch","kind":"identifier"}],"kind":"symbol","title":"MXLPitch","url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlpitch","type":"topic","abstract":[{"text":"Pitch is represented as a combination of the step of the diatonic scale, the chromatic alteration, and the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"octave.","type":"text"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLPitch"},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLDirection/voice":{"kind":"symbol","role":"symbol","fragments":[{"text":"let","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"voice","kind":"identifier"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"MXLVoice","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:7IvorMXL8MXLVoiceV"},{"text":"?","kind":"text"}],"type":"topic","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A voice is a sequence of musical events (e.g. notes, chords, rests) that proceeds linearly in time. The voice"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"element is used to distinguish between multiple voices in individual parts. It is defined within a group due"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"to its multiple uses within the MusicXML schema."}],"url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxldirection\/voice","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLDirection\/voice","title":"voice"},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLDirection/listening":{"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"let"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"listening"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:7IvorMXL12MXLListeningV","kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"MXLListening"},{"kind":"text","text":"?"}],"type":"topic","role":"symbol","title":"listening","kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLDirection\/listening","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Specifies how a score-following or machine-listening application should interact with a performer, from this"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"point in the performance onward."}],"url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxldirection\/listening"},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLDirection/Equatable-Implementations":{"type":"topic","role":"collectionGroup","title":"Equatable Implementations","kind":"article","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLDirection\/Equatable-Implementations","abstract":[],"url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxldirection\/equatable-implementations"},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLDirection/init(id:kind:offset:footnote:level:voice:staff:sound:listening:placement:isDirective:system:)":{"type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxldirection\/init(id:kind:offset:footnote:level:voice:staff:sound:listening:placement:isdirective:system:)","kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLDirection\/init(id:kind:offset:footnote:level:voice:staff:sound:listening:placement:isDirective:system:)","title":"init(id:kind:offset:footnote:level:voice:staff:sound:listening:placement:isDirective:system:)","role":"symbol","fragments":[{"text":"init","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"(","kind":"text"},{"text":"id","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:SS","text":"String","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":"?, ","kind":"text"},{"text":"kind","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": [","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:7IvorMXL12MXLDirectionV4KindV","text":"Kind","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":"], ","kind":"text"},{"text":"offset","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:7IvorMXL9MXLOffsetV","text":"MXLOffset","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":"?, ","kind":"text"},{"text":"footnote","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:7IvorMXL16MXLFormattedTextV","text":"MXLFormattedText","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":"?, ","kind":"text"},{"text":"level","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:7IvorMXL8MXLLevelV","text":"MXLLevel","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":"?, ","kind":"text"},{"text":"voice","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:7IvorMXL8MXLVoiceV","text":"MXLVoice","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":"?, ","kind":"text"},{"text":"staff","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:7IvorMXL8MXLStaffV","text":"MXLStaff","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":"?, ","kind":"text"},{"text":"sound","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:7IvorMXL8MXLSoundV","text":"MXLSound","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":"?, ","kind":"text"},{"text":"listening","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:7IvorMXL12MXLListeningV","text":"MXLListening","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":"?, ","kind":"text"},{"text":"placement","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:7IvorMXL13MXLAboveBelowO","text":"MXLAboveBelow","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":"?, ","kind":"text"},{"text":"isDirective","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:Sb","text":"Bool","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":"?, ","kind":"text"},{"text":"system","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"MXLSystemRelation","preciseIdentifier":"s:7IvorMXL17MXLSystemRelationO","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":"?)","kind":"text"}],"abstract":[{"text":"Creates a new ","type":"text"},{"code":"MXLDirection","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":".","type":"text"}]},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLDirection/isDirective":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLDirection\/isDirective","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A Boolean value indicating whether this direction is a directive, changing its default horizontal position so"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"its left-hand side aligns with the left-hand side of the time signature (or, if no time signature is present,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"the first music notational element in the measure). A default-x, justify, or halign attribute, if present,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"overrides this."}],"url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxldirection\/isdirective","kind":"symbol","title":"isDirective","type":"topic","fragments":[{"text":"let","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"isDirective","kind":"identifier"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Bool","preciseIdentifier":"s:Sb","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":"?","kind":"text"}],"role":"symbol"},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLDirection/placement":{"fragments":[{"text":"let","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"placement","kind":"identifier"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"MXLAboveBelow","preciseIdentifier":"s:7IvorMXL13MXLAboveBelowO","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":"?","kind":"text"}],"kind":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxldirection\/placement","role":"symbol","type":"topic","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The placement attribute indicates whether something is above or below another element, such as a note or a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"notation."}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLDirection\/placement","title":"placement"},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLRest":{"role":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"MXLRest","kind":"identifier"}],"fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"MXLRest","kind":"identifier"}],"kind":"symbol","title":"MXLRest","url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlrest","type":"topic","abstract":[{"text":"The rest element indicates notated rests or silences. Rest elements are usually empty, but placement on the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"staff can be specified using display-step and display-octave elements. If the measure attribute is set to yes,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"this indicates this is a complete measure rest.","type":"text"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLRest"},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLDirection/id":{"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"let"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"id"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:SS","kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"String"},{"kind":"text","text":"?"}],"type":"topic","role":"symbol","title":"id","kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLDirection\/id","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The optional-unique-id attribute group allows an element to optionally specify an ID that is unique to the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"entire document. This attribute group is not used for a required id attribute, or for an id attribute that"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"specifies an id reference."}],"url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxldirection\/id"},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLDirection/system":{"role":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxldirection\/system","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLDirection\/system","fragments":[{"text":"let","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"system","kind":"identifier"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"MXLSystemRelation","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:7IvorMXL17MXLSystemRelationO"},{"text":"?","kind":"text"}],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The system-relation attribute group distinguishes elements that are associated with a system rather than the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"particular part where the element appears."}],"kind":"symbol","type":"topic","title":"system"},"doc://IvorMXL/s9EscapableP":{"type":"unresolvable","title":"Swift.Escapable","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/s9EscapableP"},"doc://IvorMXL/s16SendableMetatypeP":{"type":"unresolvable","title":"Swift.SendableMetatype","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/s16SendableMetatypeP"},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLDirection/staff":{"type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxldirection\/staff","title":"staff","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The staff element is defined within a group due to its use by both notes and direction elements."}],"role":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLDirection\/staff","fragments":[{"text":"let","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"staff","kind":"identifier"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:7IvorMXL8MXLStaffV","text":"MXLStaff","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":"?","kind":"text"}],"kind":"symbol"},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLDirection/sound":{"kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLDirection\/sound","abstract":[{"text":"General playback parameters associated with this direction.","type":"text"}],"url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxldirection\/sound","type":"topic","role":"symbol","title":"sound","fragments":[{"text":"let","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"sound","kind":"identifier"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:7IvorMXL8MXLSoundV","text":"MXLSound","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":"?","kind":"text"}]},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLBarline":{"role":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlbarline","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLBarline","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"MXLBarline"}],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"If a barline is other than a normal single barline, it should be represented by a barline type that describes"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"it. This includes information about repeats and multiple endings, as well as line style. Barline data is on"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"the same level as the other musical data in a score — a child of a measure in a partwise score, or a part in a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"timewise score. This allows for barlines within measures, as in dotted barlines that subdivide measures in"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"complex meters. The two fermata elements allow for fermatas on both sides of the barline (the lower one"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"inverted)."}],"kind":"symbol","type":"topic","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"MXLBarline"}],"title":"MXLBarline"},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLDirection/footnote":{"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"let"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"footnote"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:7IvorMXL16MXLFormattedTextV","kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"MXLFormattedText"},{"kind":"text","text":"?"}],"type":"topic","role":"symbol","title":"footnote","kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLDirection\/footnote","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The footnote element specifies editorial information that appears in footnotes in the printed score. It is"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"defined within a group due to its multiple uses within the MusicXML schema."}],"url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxldirection\/footnote"},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLDirection/kind-swift.property":{"role":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxldirection\/kind-swift.property","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLDirection\/kind-swift.property","fragments":[{"text":"let","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"kind","kind":"identifier"},{"text":": [","kind":"text"},{"text":"Kind","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:7IvorMXL12MXLDirectionV4KindV"},{"text":"]","kind":"text"}],"kind":"symbol","abstract":[{"text":"The direction-type elements that make up this direction.","type":"text"}],"type":"topic","title":"kind"},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLSound":{"role":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlsound","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLSound","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"MXLSound"}],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The sound element contains general playback parameters. They can stand alone within a part\/measure, or be a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"component element within a direction."}],"kind":"symbol","type":"topic","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"MXLSound"}],"title":"MXLSound"}}}